  "_comment": "Wild spawn tables per land. count = wild Pokémon in that land at match start (there are no wild respawns: these are all the wilds a match has, plus fishing); levels = [min, max] for its common Pokémon, an entry's own levels override that. weight sets how often an entry is picked, relative to the others it competes with: about 8-10 common, 4-6 uncommon, 2-3 scarce, 1.2 rare. Lands with \"use\": \"nearest\" (meadows, beaches, the castle grounds) take each spot's table from the nearest of the four lands. Levels also rise toward the Shadow Crystal: + centerLevelBonus x (1 - distance / centerLevelRadius)^curve (config.json wild). An entry with a habitat only spawns in that habitat (see habitats): each land fills habitatSlots of its count there, rolling only among its own habitat entries; every other spot rolls among the entries with no habitat. Stronger encounters (strong) are separate from these tables.",
